## rc-units | Units and constants check | physics | 1 | phys1 | rc-phys1
quiz 2 | Unit of magnetic field strength (B)?
* Tesla
o Weber
o Henry
o Gauss only
= 1 T = 10,000 gauss. Earth's field is about 50 μT.
> Next

quiz 3 | Unit of pressure?
* Pascal
o Newton
o Joule
o Bar only
= 1 Pa = 1 N/m². Atmospheric pressure ≈ 101 kPa.
> Next

quiz 3 | Planck's constant h is approximately…
* 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J s
o 6.67 × 10⁻¹¹ N m²/kg²
o 1.38 × 10⁻²³ J/K
o 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ kg
= The others: G, Boltzmann's constant, and the electron mass.
> Next

quiz 3 | Boltzmann's constant k_B is approximately…
* 1.38 × 10⁻²³ J/K
o 6.02 × 10²³
o 8.31 J/(mol K)
o 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ C
= R = N_A k_B ≈ 8.31 J/(mol K).
> Next

quiz 3 | Mass of a proton?
* About 1.67 × 10⁻²⁷ kg
o About 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ kg
o About 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ kg
o About 6.6 × 10⁻²⁷ kg
= About 1,836 times the electron's mass.
> Next

quiz 4 | 1 electronvolt in joules?
* 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ J
o 1 J
o 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁶ J
o 9.1 × 10⁻³¹ J
= The energy of one electron accelerated through 1 V.
> Next

quiz 4 | Permittivity of free space ε₀ is approximately…
* 8.85 × 10⁻¹² F/m
o 4π × 10⁻⁷ H/m
o 9 × 10⁹ N m²/C²
o 6.67 × 10⁻¹¹ N m²/kg²
= μ₀ is 4π × 10⁻⁷ H/m (very nearly). 1/(4πε₀) is the 9 × 10⁹.
> Next

quiz 4 | The fine-structure constant α is approximately…
* 1/137
o 1/1000
o 1/2
o 137
= Dimensionless: e²/(4πε₀ħc).
> Next

quiz 4 | Gravitational constant G?
* 6.67 × 10⁻¹¹ N m²/kg²
o 9.8 m/s²
o 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J s
o 3 × 10⁸ m/s
= The least precisely known fundamental constant.
> Next

quiz 4 | Stefan–Boltzmann law: total power radiated by a black body scales as…
* T⁴
o T
o T²
o 1/T
= Double the temperature, 16 times the power.
> Next

quiz 4 | Wien's law: peak wavelength of black-body radiation scales as…
* 1/T
o T
o T⁴
o √T
= The Sun (about 5,800 K) peaks around 500 nm.
> Next

quiz 4 | Speed of light in vacuum in km/s, roughly?
* 300,000 km/s
o 30,000 km/s
o 3,000 km/s
o 3,000,000 km/s
= Around the Earth about 7.5 times in one second.
> Next

quiz 4 | 1 light-year in metres, roughly?
* 9.5 × 10¹⁵ m
o 3 × 10⁸ m
o 1.5 × 10¹¹ m
o 3 × 10¹⁶ m
= 1.5 × 10¹¹ m is the Earth–Sun distance (1 AU). A parsec is about 3.1 × 10¹⁶ m.
> Next

quiz 4 | Avogadro's number connects…
* Moles to number of particles
o Energy to temperature
o Charge to current
o Mass to energy
= 6.022 × 10²³ per mole.
> Next

quiz 5 | The reduced Planck constant ħ equals…
* h/2π
o 2πh
o h²
o h/2
= ≈ 1.055 × 10⁻³⁴ J s.
> Units check complete

## rc-maths | Maths facts check | maths | 1 | calc1 | rc-calc2
quiz 2 | sin²θ + cos²θ = ?
* 1
o 0
o 2
o tan²θ
= Pythagoras on the unit circle.
> Next

quiz 3 | What's cos(0)?
* 1
o 0
o −1
o 1/2
= Cosine starts at its maximum.
> Next

quiz 3 | e^(ln 5) = ?
* 5
o ln 5
o e⁵
o 1/5
= They're inverse functions.
> Next

quiz 3 | ln(1) = ?
* 0
o 1
o e
o Undefined
= e⁰ = 1.
> Next

quiz 3 | Quadratic formula roots of ax² + bx + c = 0?
* (−b ± √(b² − 4ac))/(2a)
o (b ± √(b² + 4ac))/(2a)
o −b/(2a)
o (−b ± √(b − 4ac))/a
= b² − 4ac is the discriminant.
> Next

quiz 4 | tan(45°) = ?
* 1
o 0
o √3
o Undefined
= Opposite equals adjacent.
> Next

quiz 4 | The derivative of arctan x at x = 0?
* 1
o 0
o 1/2
o π/4
= 1/(1 + x²) at 0.
> Next

quiz 4 | log₁₀(0.001) = ?
* −3
o 3
o −2
o 0.001
= 10⁻³.
> Next

quiz 4 | How many radians in 180°?
* π
o 2π
o π/2
o 180
= 360° = 2π radians.
> Next

quiz 4 | |3 + 4i| = ?
* 5
o 7
o 1
o 25
= √(9 + 16).
> Facts check complete
